\description{
zfbehavior analyzes zebrafish larval light-dark transition test (LDTT)
tracking data and developmental toxicity, from vendor files to hit calls
and benchmark concentrations (BMC). The workflow has five modules; each is
run by one or more Agent Skills that guide a coding agent (or a person)
through one run folder per step, with a rendered Quarto report.
}
\section{Modules}{

\itemize{
\item \link{module1} Data import and consistency checks. Skill
\code{dataset-import-qc}.
\item \link{module2} Raw-response visualization and inter-plate VC QC.
Skills \code{raw-response-plots}, \code{interplate-vc-qc}.
\item \link{module3} Endpoint calculation, normalization, and intra-plate VC
QC. Skills \code{behavior-endpoints}, \code{intraplate-vc-qc},
\code{devtox-endpoints}.
\item \link{module4} ANOVA / repeated-measures ANOVA hit calling. Skill
\code{behavior-endpoints-anova}.
\item \link{module5} Curvep-based BMC modeling of behavioral and
developmental toxicity endpoints. Skills \code{behavior-endpoints-bmc},
\code{devtox-endpoints-bmc}.
}
}

